issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducable in 4.4.1-stable and 4.5-beta5\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 745 - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-4790 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 7.95 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI have a MeshInstance3D with a PlaneMesh. I need to get a section of an image onto the mesh, so I tried using a AtlasTexture in a StandardMaterial3D, but it doesn't display anything. I reloaded the project and now it displays the whole image on the mesh, but not a section, just the whole thing.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n_(Open the MRP and see the README or follow these steps in a new project)_\n1. Create a MeshInstance3D node\n2. Add a PlaneMesh or QuadMesh (I used a PlaneMesh)\n3. Add a StandardMaterial3D to the material property\n4. Add an AtlasTexture to the albedo_texture property\n5. Add an image to the atlas property of the AtlasTexture\n6. Select the region (don't make it the whole image)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[AtlasTextureBug-MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21674077/AtlasTextureBug-MRP.zip)\n_See README in the above file_","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}